goals:
- small
- retargetable
- portable (no external dependencies and minimal libc dependencies)
- complete toolchain
  - compiler & assembler
  - linker
  - interpreter (compile & load)
  - build system
  - package manager

why not:
- clang
  - massive
  - lacks build system & package manager
- tinycc
  - complex codebase
  - lacks optimization
  - lacks build system & package manager
- golang
  - probably closes to the end goal, but still massive
  - require external dependencies

prepare:
gcc -Wall -otic -ggdb -O0 main.c core.c hash.c ia64.c arm8.c exec.c

run: ./tic <arch> <code> where arch could be "e" for inideate execution
./tic a hello.c
